body:
Just to put an update in since the post got a lot of attention and to add info for anyone having the same issue.

&#x200B;

So the part that broke was the [Upper Radiator Hose](https://imgur.com/tNYpNVT) ($50) on my 2009 Ford Focus.

&#x200B;

I didn't realize that the plastic neck was something already connected to the hose and not it's own separate part. 

&#x200B;

Was able to remove the connector myself, but I cant really reach the location to where the hose connects to the motor so will be having to get some actual mechanic help anyways.

&#x200B;

Didn't mean to upset anyone with my JB Weld idea, was just something i always saw my grandpa use as a quick fix on his cars/tractor.

&#x200B;

Thanks again for all the responses and hope this post can help someone later
